.TH HAMR 1 "2026-11-23" "hamr 0.4.6.dev4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hamr \- turn EPUB, PDF, Markdown and plain-text documents into local audiobooks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hamr
.RI [ global-options ] " command " [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hamr
reads a document, renders narration using Breeze TTS2, checks the speech
locally, and assembles a mastered, chaptered M4B with a source companion.
An unresolved source or speech finding holds publication for review.
The packaged speech engine targets Linux x86-64 with AVX2.
Windows x64 CPU Q8 has passed checked publication and interruption
recovery. Windows Vulkan is a preview.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-home " DIRECTORY"
Use this app state directory. Place this option before the command.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print versioned structured results. Supply explicit selections when
a command would otherwise prompt. Progress appears on standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show commands. Use
.BI "hamr " "command " \-\-help
for command-specific options.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B "settings"
Show the reading preferences for new books. Use
.B "hamr settings --performance off --mode study"
to save plain technical reading. Expressive listening uses
.BR "--performance auto --mode listen" .
.TP
.B "setup"
Choose a recommended profile and download the speech engine and offline
speech checks. Use
.BI \-\-profile " PROFILE"
for explicit selection,
.B \-\-checks-only
to add speech checks without choosing an engine profile, or
.B \-\-engine-only
to configure just speech generation.
.B \-\-ocr-only
sets up English scanned-PDF OCR with the installed Tesseract executable.
Use
.B \-\-ocr-profile auto
to add OCR during ordinary setup.
.B \-\-wash-only
sets up local voice preparation. Use
.BI \-\-wash-profile " PROFILE"
to choose an exact preparation profile.
.TP
.B "doctor, profiles"
Describe this installation and hardware, or list speech profiles.
.TP
.B "voice cast, voice sample, voice select"
List the cast, preview an included introduction, or save a narrator
for new books. Use
.B "voice sample CHARACTER \-\-play"
to listen. Breeze uses the separate source-based references and transcripts.
.B "voice list, voice clone, voice design"
manage custom voices.
.B "voice clone"
saves the original reference and a reusable 24 kHz reference. It applies
qualified installed cleanup when needed and reports the selection.
Use
.B \-\-wash off
for direct import or
.BI \-\-wash " PROFILE"
to request an installed treatment. Use
.BI \-\-channel " NUMBER"
to choose a source channel numbered from one.
.TP
.BI "open " DOCUMENT
Review the plan, render, check and assemble a book.
Use
.BI \-\-voice " cast:CHARACTER"
to select a voice for this book,
.B \-\-yes
to confirm in advance, and
.B \-\-play
to play the finished book. Omit
.BI \-\-output " DIRECTORY"
to write under ~/Audiobooks. Use
.B \-\-mastering off
to keep the original playback level on a new or queued book.
.TP
.B "plan, profile, queue, worker"
Inspect a proposed reading, save reading preferences, create a queued
job, or process the queue.
.B "worker \-\-once \-\-json"
reports each job handled in that pass. A failure exits 2 and a review
hold exits 3 when no job failed. Use
.B "hamr status JOB"
for the saved reason and recovery command.
.TP
.BI "resume " JOB
Continue a saved job using verified takes and speech observations.
.B "render"
also runs the full workflow by default. Use
.B \-\-max-new-takes
for a manual render batch.
.B "run"
exposes pipeline options.
.TP
.B "status, show, preview, excerpt, play"
Inspect jobs or source locations, audition a passage, export saved
takes, or play a ready book. For a publication hold,
.B "status JOB"
shows the planned output file and whether to resume the automatic
speech check or review a specific passage.
.TP
.B "repair, qa, review"
Apply a scoped correction, compare speech to the plan, or record and
resolve a listening finding.
Use
.B "hamr repair JOB --mastering natural"
followed by
.B "hamr resume JOB --no-synthesis"
to master a new edition from the saved and checked recordings.
The default mastering applies one gain to the whole book and checks the
encoded playback peaks. Timing and the previous edition are preserved.
.TP
.B "pause, cancel, cleanup"
Mark an idle job paused or cancelled, or inspect unreferenced data.
Cleanup previews changes unless
.B \-\-apply
is supplied. Published output is kept.
.TP
.BI "completion " SHELL
Print completion for Bash, Zsh or Fish.
.SH DOCUMENT INTAKE
An image directory or ZIP of loose page images is one book. The plan follows
the order in a page manifest or sorts filenames naturally. An archive
containing several books presents entry IDs. Use \fB\-\-entry ID\fR to select
one supported publication.
.PP
A NIMAS ZIP, extracted source folder, or package OPF opens in its declared
reading order. DTBook XML can also be opened directly. Printed page labels
stay in the source companion.
.PP
Text-bearing DAISY 3 source folders, OPFs and ZIPs follow the declared
SMIL sequence. Existing media remains recoverable from the original package.
.PP
Text-bearing DAISY 2.02 source folders, NCC documents and ZIPs follow
synchronized HTML text in playback order. Open a component SMIL to read
that section. Authored notes follow the usual note settings.
.PP
JATS articles in XML files, folders or ZIPs read their primary abstract,
body, linked footnotes and authored figure descriptions. The source
companion retains the article and its declared local assets.
.PP
TEI editions read the authored main text and linked notes. The source
companion retains alternate witness readings and declared local assets.
.PP
BITS books and chapter exports use the authored headings, notes and local
XML includes. Open an NCBI Bookshelf archive or extracted directory to
read the chapter order in its table of contents.
.PP
Open a DocBook manual, chapter, or reference entry as XML, a source
folder, or an archive. Local XML includes establish the reading order.
Authored descriptions, linked notes, and simple CALS tables are read from
the source. Publisher variables can be resolved in a prepared edition.
.PP
FictionBook 2 and 3 preserve authored notes and verse lines. Open a
FictionBook 3 file, ZIP archive, or extracted publication. Its package
declarations identify the text and linked original assets.
.PP
Use \fB\-\-offline\fR with \fBopen\fR, \fBplan\fR, or \fBqueue\fR to
use resident or already installed readers only. Use \fBresume JOB\fR to
continue a saved intake.
.PP
For plain text, reStructuredText, TextBundle, or compiled HTML Help with a known character encoding, pass
\fB\-\-encoding NAME\fR, for example \fB\-\-encoding windows-1252\fR.
.PP
.B hamr source BOOK_DIRECTORY LOCATION_ID --output FILE
recovers the original file or archive member from a finished book folder.
Use the location or passage ID from source.html. Keep the original file
and companion together when moving a book.
.SH CONTEXT REVIEW
Ambiguous readings use the automatic policy by default.
Use
.BI \-\-context\-review " FILE"
to supply a local array of candidate replies, or
.BI \-\-context\-review\-endpoint " URL"
to request a review from a loopback HTTP service.
The service may request one follow-up with bounded source context.
Accepted choices are saved with the job.
.SH PERFORMANCE
.B \-\-performance
selects
.BR auto " (the default) or " off .
Automatic delivery follows source cues in EPUB, searchable or scanned PDF,
Markdown, and plain text on the built-in Breeze engine. It supports dialogue
delivery, authored sounds, and heading cadence. In study or procedure mode
it can also guide the delivery of a complete table or equation. Use
.B "hamr preview JOB --utterance ID --play"
to hear the effective request. Speech recognition can flag a directed
take for listening review while preserving the original take.
.TP
.B "hamr preview JOB --utterance ID --compare FILE"
Read named settings from a JSON object and render alternate takes of the
same passage. An empty settings object uses the saved request. Override
the seed, instruction, markers, guidance, or sampling. The command records
the exact Breeze requests and WAV hashes in a local manifest.
Add --play to hear the results in order. Comparisons leave the job
and any published book intact.
.TP
.B "hamr setup --checks-only --asr-profile auto"
Set up offline verification independently of the speech engine. Auto selects
a qualified verifier by platform, available system memory and disk space.
Choose fluid-int8 or whisper explicitly. Doctor reports the active verifier
and its recommendation. Ordinary open and resume use the selected verifier.
From a source checkout, use
.B "uv run hamr setup --checks-only"
with the same state directory as the book command.
.TP
.B "hamr transcribe INPUT"
Compare the active verifier and a second local recognizer on an audio excerpt of up to
125 seconds. Supply a job ID and
.B --utterance
to check the exact committed passage. The command leaves job state untouched.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed. Use
.B "hamr status JOB"
to check the state of a saved job.
.TP
.B 2
Command or input error.
.TP
.B 3
Publication is held for an automatic speech check or a review finding.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted. Committed work can be resumed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HAMR_HOME
Default app state directory. The legacy
.B AUDIOBOOK_HOME
also works. Explicit
.B \-\-home
takes priority.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hamr
Default state, including models, snapshots and verified takes.
Existing owned legacy installations can use
.IR ~/.local/share/audiobook .
.TP
.I ~/Audiobooks/JOB-rREV/book.m4b
Default published audiobook path. The folder also contains
the source and companion files.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up once. Accept the recommended profile at the prompt.
.PP
.nf
hamr setup
hamr voice sample nigel-thornberry \-\-play
hamr open "$HOME/Downloads/My book.epub" \e
  \-\-voice cast:nigel-thornberry
.fi
.PP
If interrupted, use the job ID printed by hamr.
.PP
.nf
hamr status
hamr resume JOB
hamr play JOB
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR mpv (1)
.PP
.UR https://github.com/MimirLab/hamr
Project and full usage guide
